# But don't send Pixel Streaming to 2,000 viewers

One Unreal instance should produce **one programme feed**.

Then distribute that feed.

And something extremely timely just launched: Cloudflare Stream's new WebRTC live system now supports **sub-second WHIP/WHEP broadcasting to thousands of viewers**. ([Cloudflare Docs][9])

So eventually:

```text
Unreal GPU
   │
   │ one programme feed
   ▼
Cloudflare Stream
   │
   ├── viewer 1
   ├── viewer 2
   ├── viewer 3
   │
   └── viewer 2000
```

Cloudflare says current WebRTC delivery pricing, beginning October 15, is **$1 / 1,000 viewer-minutes**. ([Cloudflare Docs][9])

Thus 2,000 viewers × 30 minutes ≈ **$60 delivery**.

Much better than making 2,000 Unreal Pixel Streaming sessions.

LiveKit remains for the actual interactive participants.

